    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed slate today, with our primary offensive exposure limited to the matchup against Gavin Williams. Between our active starters, **Sam Antonacci** secures the higher efficiency score at 43.76, narrowly edging out **Miguel Vargas** (42.35). While both players are suppressed by the 2.95 xERA of the opposing starter\u2014an elite arm that forces us to temper our expectations\u2014**Sam Antonacci** gains a notable 7% boost from his platoon advantage. **Miguel Vargas**, meanwhile, carries the weight of a 19% skill penalty against Williams, though his projected leadoff spot provides a +10% order cushion that keeps him safely above our 40-point threshold for a marginal start.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Brayan Rocchio**, who landed just outside the starting lineup with a 38.59 score. While **Brayan Rocchio** has shown solid recency, the optimizer penalized his projected ninth-place spot in the order (-8%) and the lack of a strong platoon advantage against Sean Burke. Ultimately, he remains on the bench to preserve our game caps, as his current profile lacks the elite ceiling required to displace our primary starters on a day where the opposing pitching environment is so restrictive.\n\nBeyond the immediate lineup, the roster remains heavily impacted by external circumstances. We continue to manage the absences of **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** due to today\u2019s team off-day, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. As we look ahead, we continue to monitor the development paths of prospects like **Henry Bolte**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Luis Lara**, keeping them in reserve while **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Wade Meckler** await more favorable park factors and pitching matchups to bolster our pursuit of stolen bases and overall category efficiency.",
